# C# sprites (ME-276): clicking the coin in the World view selects it (sprites draw into the picking
# buffer); then SpriteProbe reads its SpriteRenderer and changes its sprite, flip, tint and sorting
# from C#, and the component holds the new values.
#   ./.build/Editor_Debug/Havana --scene Assets/Scenes/Tests/SpriteScriptTest.lvl --editor-exec Assets/Scenes/Tests/SpriteScriptFlows.edscript
wait-log dotnet ready | 7200
wait 30
select Coin
focus-window World View
wait 2
action View.Front
action View.FrameSelected
wait 60
select-none
pick 0.5 0.5
wait 10
assert-active Coin
play
wait-log SpriteProbe: found True, showing Coins_0, layer 1 | 600
wait-log SpriteProbe: now Coins_2 flipX True flipY False color 0.50 0.75 sorting 3/7 | 600
assert-field Coin | SpriteRenderer.SpriteName | "Coins_2"
assert-field Coin | SpriteRenderer.FlipX | true
assert-field Coin | SpriteRenderer.Opacity | 0.75 ~ 0.001
screenshot .tmp/EditorFlows/SpriteScriptFlows.png
stop
quit
